3. WaRF's clone rule (SPECIFICATION 3.1.2): every pair must disagree on >= 15 % of reviews
==============================================================================================================
  Two agents of different strictness disagree at least as often as their REJECT rates differ, even if
  they rank the reviews alike. 'Crossed' counts the disagreements where the laxer agent of the pair
  rejects and the stricter approves: 0 means one judgement at two thresholds. For scale, the count
  expected if the agents erred independently given the truth, as the SPRT assumes.

  persona_v3 (Claude Haiku 4.5): 12 reviews; REJECT share ADVOCATE 0.42, AUDITOR 0.50, BOUNDARY 0.58, SKEPTIC 0.75, TEST-FOCUSED 0.67
    rho min 0.08, mean 0.25; pairs under 0.15: 1 of 10; crossed 5 of 30 disagreements (17%); independent given the truth: 10

  h2h_auditor5 (Claude Haiku 4.5): 12 reviews; REJECT share AUDITOR-1 0.58, AUDITOR-2 0.50, AUDITOR-3 0.58, AUDITOR-4 0.67, AUDITOR-5 0.75
    rho min 0.08, mean 0.15; pairs under 0.15: 4 of 10; crossed 2 of 18 disagreements (11%); independent given the truth: 12

  h2h_skeptic5 (Claude Haiku 4.5): 12 reviews; REJECT share SKEPTIC-1 0.67, SKEPTIC-2 0.67, SKEPTIC-3 0.67, SKEPTIC-4 0.75, SKEPTIC-5 0.75
    rho min 0.08, mean 0.15; pairs under 0.15: 4 of 10; crossed 6 of 18 disagreements (33%); independent given the truth: 12

  Jev, five personas, Round 1: 100 reviews; REJECT share ADVOCATE 0.19, AUDITOR 0.49, BOUNDARY 0.13, SKEPTIC 0.21, TEST-FOCUSED 0.47
    rho min 0.08, mean 0.23; pairs under 0.15: 4 of 10; crossed 14 of 228 disagreements (6%); independent given the truth: 113

